{% set local_problem %}
<p>Athens' established neighborhoods are beautiful — mature trees lining streets, deep lots with decades-old landscaping, homes with character that newer subdivisions can't match. But all those trees create a constant stream of debris that ends up in your gutters.</p>

<p>The neighborhoods around Athens State University, near the downtown courthouse square, and throughout central Athens are particularly affected. Century-old oaks drop massive leaves every fall. Maples shed thousands of seeds in spring. Pecans scatter shells and debris year-round. By the time you've cleaned up from one season, the next one's already filling your gutters back up.</p>

<p>North Alabama receives 55+ inches of rain annually. When gutters clog, that water doesn't disappear — it overflows, runs down your siding, and pools around your foundation. Limestone County's clay-heavy soil doesn't absorb water quickly, which means pooling around your foundation can persist for days after a heavy rain, slowly working its way toward your basement or crawlspace.</p>

<p>Many Athens homeowners fall into a dangerous pattern: they know their gutters need cleaning, but life gets busy. Weeks turn into months, and by the time they get around to it, gutters are packed solid with decomposed leaves and water damage has already started. Professional cleaning breaks that cycle — we handle it quickly, thoroughly, and on a schedule that protects your home year-round.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set service_explanation %}
<p>Our gutter cleaning service is comprehensive. We start by hand-removing all debris from inside your gutters — leaves, seeds, roof grit, decomposed organic matter, and anything else that's accumulated. We don't just blow debris onto your lawn or push it toward the downspouts (a common shortcut that causes clogs downstream).</p>

<p>Next, we flush all downspouts with water to ensure they're clear and flowing properly. Downspout clogs are a common problem that many homeowners miss when attempting DIY cleaning — debris backs up in the downspout, water can't exit, and the gutter overflows even though it looks clean from above.</p>

<p>Finally, we inspect your entire gutter system: hangers, seams, slope, and the fascia boards behind. We'll flag loose hangers, developing leaks, rust spots, and fascia damage before they become expensive problems. When we're done, we clean up all debris from your landscaping — your property will look better than when we arrived.</p>
{% endset %}

{% set why_us %}
<p>We've been cleaning gutters in Athens and throughout Limestone County for over 20 years. From historic homes near the courthouse square to mid-century neighborhoods around Athens State, we've seen every type of debris problem and gutter configuration this area can produce.</p>

